# Trample (CR 702.19b) and "deals combat damage to a player": on turn 3 Bot1 puts all 3 of the Warg's damage on its
# blocker (allowed, lethal is at least 2), nothing reaches Bot2 and no trigger is asked for; on turn 5 the default
# division gives the second Ornithopter lethal 2 and tramples 1 over, which triggers it, and a Treasure appears.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Mox Emerald
Bejeweled Warg
Forest x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Ornithopter
Forest x12

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Bejeweled Warg.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Bejeweled Warg)
Bot2.Block(Ornithopter > Bejeweled Warg)
Bot1.AssignDamage(Bejeweled Warg > Ornithopter: 3)
! Bot1.Modes
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot2.Life = 20
? Bot2.Battlefield.Count = 1
? Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 3
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Bejeweled Warg)
Bot2.Block(Ornithopter > Bejeweled Warg)
Bot1.Modes(Create a Treasure token)
[T5 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 19
Bot2.Battlefield.Count = 0
Bot1.Battlefield = Forest; Mox Emerald; Bejeweled Warg; Treasure Token
